      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1497",
      "html": "<p>Delturus parahybae Eigenmann &amp; Eigenmann, 1889. Family Loricariidae. Size: 210 mm (8.3 inches) SL. Etymology: Deltos = small board (Greek) + oura = tail (Greek). IUCN Red List: Critically Endangered (last assessed 2018).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1497",
      "html": "<p>South America: Paraíba do Sul River basin, Rio de Janeiro State rivers, Brazil. Type locality: Rio Parahyba do Sul, between Barra do Piraí and Trés Rios, Rio de Janeiro state, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
